# S6 — DOES IT READ AS A HOUSE?
#
# The whole ladder in one script: flat ground, a house placed from the pose (S4,
# four walls that meet), a door and a window cut into it (S5), and the roof the
# house now carries (S6). Then stand back and look, which is the only test that
# answers the question this step asks.
#
# ⚠ THE DOOR AND THE WINDOW WERE CUT FROM INSIDE THE HOUSE AND CUT NOTHING, for as
# long as this script has existed. Both poses answered *"no wall here to open —
# stand against one"*, in BOTH drivers, so `s6-house.png` never had either. It was
# the pose, not the gesture: the two below are on the house's own perimeter and are
# measured, not guessed — `opened profile 1 at (-2,1)` and `opened profile 2 at
# (-1,2)` come back on the wire.
#
# ⚠ AND THE CAMERA IS NO LONGER THE CHARACTER. `eye` stands it in the world looking
# back at whoever is standing there, so the last two shots can show the house from
# outside WITH its author in the doorway — which is what the acceptance question
# actually asks. Before this, every picture in this tree was taken from behind the
# person building it.

echo --- flat ground to build on
at 0 0 0
key ArrowUp
wait rebuilt

echo --- a house, facing one of the six the lattice can mitre
at -6 -6 30
key H

echo --- a door and a window in its near wall (stand ON the wall's own cells)
at -3 2 30
key O
at -1 3 30
key P

# ⚠ THE AUTHOR STEPS OUT BEFORE THEY ARE PHOTOGRAPHED, and the first attempt is why:
# aimed at the pose that CUT the door — hard against the wall's own cells — the eye
# looked at a figure the wall was standing in front of. In frame and invisible, which
# the projection arithmetic cannot tell apart from visible. So the shot moves them
# clear of the wall first, and then the house is BEHIND them, which is the picture the
# acceptance question is about.
# ⚠ AND THE EYE GOES OFF THE CHARACTER→HOUSE AXIS, which is a composition rule
# rather than a taste: standing the eye on that line puts a 1.8-unit figure against
# a 9-unit building at the same bearing, and it reads as part of the wall. Three
# angles were photographed; the one that shows a PERSON is the one across the line.
echo --- the author outside their own house, from across the line
at -6 5 30
eye -18 -6 7
snap s6-house

echo --- and square on to the door they just cut
eye -13 12 5
snap s6-door

eye off
